Subject: VMS: mch_get_shellsize() fails when the size is unknown

When SYS$OUTPUT is not a terminal, get_tty()'s SENSEMODE fails and returns
a width and page length of 0. mch_get_shellsize() still set Rows and
Columns from them and returned OK, and check_shellsize() then made the
screen as small as Vim allows (2 lines of 12 columns): with --not-a-term
and output to a file, as upstream's test suite runs, every test failed with
"E36: Not enough room". Return FAIL and keep the old size instead, as
os_unix.c does.

--- a/src/os_vms.c
+++ b/src/os_vms.c
@@ -205,6 +205,11 @@
     TT_MODE	tmode;
 
     tmode = get_tty();			// get size from VMS
+    // Not a terminal (output to a file or a mailbox): the size is unknown.
+    // Keep the old values (80 x 24 at first), as os_unix.c does; 0 x 0 would
+    // become the smallest possible screen.
+    if (tmode.width == 0 || tmode.x.y.length == 0)
+	return FAIL;
     Columns = tmode.width;
     Rows = tmode.x.y.length;
     return OK;
